F3 (advisory) — a gap class this branch names but does not file
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The production lex clause adopted *in this very commit* says a gap found in
the tooling becomes a lesson or a backlog opus within the cascade that found
it, never handoff prose alone. This branch names three CLI gaps. Searched
all seven backlog opera titles, `grep -rn addressed_by packages/cli/src`
(non-test), and the verb list `bisellium` prints:
  - no per-opus halt verb (D-017, and both halted opera's `blocked_on`) —
    NO backlog opus, NO lesson. Recorded only in decision/handoff prose.
  - no verb stamping `addressed_by` on a lesson — retro.ts only *reads* it
    (retro.ts:115), nothing writes it, so this commit's three stamps are
    hand-written lesson front matter — NO backlog opus, NO lesson.
  - no verb re-stamping identity onto an existing gate (D-018) — covered,
    W-040 "gate correction: re-sign a wrongly-signed gate without erasing
    it". No action needed on this one.
Two instances, not three. Both want a one-line backlog opus (or a lesson)
before the cascade closes, or the clause is dead on its first day.

F4 (advisory) — see section 4, D-005 cites no lesson id.

